<!-- SPECIAL CASES -->
<div class="section-label">Troubleshooting</div>
<div class="section-title">Special Cases</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ The hearing aid is still under warranty</h3>
<p>The customer shouldn't pay for a repair that's already covered.</p>
<ol>
<li>Don't send it to Signia as a paid repair. Add a note with the warranty end date shown in Signia.</li>
<li>Message Rhett. Usually the customer gets a refund and the repair is processed as a free warranty repair.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ The customer actually LOST the hearing aid</h3>
<p>The Repair product doesn't cover loss.</p>
<ol>
<li>If it's <strong>out of warranty</strong>: loss isn't covered. The customer needs a new hearing aid at standard pricing. Message Rhett about a refund and offer to book a consultation.</li>
<li>If it's <strong>in warranty</strong>: it can be replaced for a <strong>$299 fee per aid</strong> (pending Andrea's confirmation). Message Rhett to sort out the payment, then order the loss replacement in the Signia portal.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ Signia says the hearing aid can't be repaired</h3>
<ol>
<li>Add a note with what Signia said, and leave the card in <strong>Received - Sent to Signia</strong>.</li>
<li>Message Rhett. The options are usually a refund or a new hearing aid quote.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ The hearing aid hasn't arrived</h3>
<ol>
<li>If the card has been in <strong>Registered - Awaiting Shipment</strong> for about a week with no aid received, call or text the customer.</li>
<li>Check they got the shipping instructions email (look in <span class="click">Conversations</span>). Resend the instructions if needed.</li>
<li>Add a note with what you found.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ I moved the card to Repaired before entering the date</h3>
<p>The customer already got a message with a blank or wrong date, and it <strong>will not resend</strong>.</p>
<ol>
<li>Enter the correct <strong>Warranty End Date</strong> on the contact and save.</li>
<li>Open the contact's <span class="click">Conversations</span> and send this SMS by hand:</li>
</ol>
<div class="sms-box">
<div class="sms-label">Correction SMS (send manually)</div>
Hi [first name], correction from Hearing Benefit Services: your 6-month repair warranty runs until [date]. Sorry for any confusion! Questions? Call us at 808-435-7002.
</div>
<ol start="3">
<li>Add a note on the contact: "Sent corrected repair warranty end date [date]."</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>📞 The customer calls asking about their repair</h3>
<p>Open their card in <strong>Opportunities → Signia Repair</strong>. The stage tells you exactly where they are:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="info-table">
<thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What to Tell Them</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Purchased - Awaiting Registration</td><td>"We still need your hearing aid details." Help them submit the form.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registered - Awaiting Shipment</td><td>"We're waiting for your hearing aid to arrive." Confirm they have the shipping instructions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Received - Sent to Signia</td><td>"We received it and it's being repaired. We'll text and email you when it's on its way back."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repaired - Returned to Customer</td><td>"It's been repaired!" Read them the <strong>Warranty End Date</strong> and mention the 12-month extension offer.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Needs Review</td><td>"We're looking into your registration and will contact you shortly."</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>🔧 The repaired hearing aid breaks again within 6 months</h3>
<ol>
<li>Confirm today is <strong>before</strong> their <strong>Warranty End Date</strong> (and they have the tag <code>repair-complete</code>).</li>
<li>If covered: process it through Signia as a warranty repair. <strong>No charge to the customer.</strong> Add a note.</li>
<li>If it's lost instead of broken, see "The customer actually LOST the hearing aid" above. The 6-month repair warranty doesn't cover loss.</li>
</ol>
</div>

